course: dictionary
lesson: 11091
title: A whaler is a ship or a person
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A whaler is a word with more than one meaning. The dictionary gives three: a ship used for hunting whales, a person who hunts whales, and a long, narrow rowing boat called a whaleboat. Read the words around it to find out which one is meant.
explain: «Grey whales feed by sucking mud from the seabed and sifting out small creatures; in Mexican lagoons some now come up to boats and let people touch them, though whalers once called them devil fish.» Here whalers are people who hunted whales, because the sentence is about animals that were hunted. Ask yourself what would fit: a hunter fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: Whalers belong mostly to history lessons and old stories, such as «Moby-Dick». Whalers once hunted whales for oil, meat and bone. Today most countries have banned commercial whaling to protect whales, though a few countries still allow some.
fact: A whaler can mean a ship, a person, or a whaleboat, so check the sentence to see which.
fact: «Whaler» means a ship or a person that hunts whales.
fact: Whalers once hunted whales for oil, meat and bone.
fact: Most countries have now banned commercial whaling to protect whales.
fact: Nantucket in the USA and Hobart in Australia were whaling ports, where whaling ships sailed from.
exercise: What did whalers once hunt? | Penguins | Seals | Sharks | *Whales
exercise: In «though whalers once called them devil fish», what does whalers mean? | Sailors who sang songs at sea | Shops that sold fish | Animals that live in mud | *People who hunted whales
exercise: Whalers got oil, meat and what else from whales? | *Bone | Feathers | Shells | Sand
test: Which of these was a whaling port in history? | Cairo in Egypt | Paris in France | *Hobart in Australia
test: What is a whaleboat? | A huge net for catching fish | *A long, narrow rowing boat | A shop that sold whale meat | A bird that lives near water
exam: Why do most countries now ban commercial whaling? | *To protect whales | To build more whaling ships | To make more whale oil | To feed the whalers
